            {
              "id": "SNYK-ALPINE324-BROTLI-21483816",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Critical severity - CVE-2026-111497 vulnerability in brotli"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "(CVE-2026-111497) brotli/brotli-libs@1.2.0-r1"
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "",
                "markdown": "## NVD Description\n**_Note:_** _Versions mentioned in the description apply only to the upstream `brotli` package and not the `brotli` package as distributed by `Alpine`._\n_See `How to fix?` for `Alpine:3.24` relevant fixed versions and status._\n\nA buffer overflow vulnerability in the Brotli decoder (c/dec/decode.c) in Google Brotli versions 1.0.3 through 1.2.0 on all platforms allows a remote unauthenticated attacker to corrupt adjacent decoder state memory, disclose sensitive memory contents, cause a denial of service, or potentially execute arbitrary code using a crafted Brotli-compressed stream.\n\n\n\n\n\nUsers need to update any Brotli libraries or binaries between 1.0.3 through 1.2.0 to the latest available version: 1.0.10 or 1.1.1 or 1.2.1.\n## Remediation\nUpgrade `Alpine:3.24` `brotli` to version 1.2.1-r0 or higher.\n## References\n- [https://github.com/andybalholm/brotli/releases/tag/v1.2.7](https://github.com/andybalholm/brotli/releases/tag/v1.2.7)\n- [https://nodejs.org/en/blog/vulnerability/october-2026-security-releases#nodejs-brotli-decoder-out-of-bounds-write-permits-remote-code-execution-cve-2026-111497---high](https://nodejs.org/en/blog/vulnerability/october-2026-security-releases#nodejs-brotli-decoder-out-of-bounds-write-permits-remote-code-execution-cve-2026-111497---high)\n- [http://www.openwall.com/lists/oss-security/2026/10/23/25](http://www.openwall.com/lists/oss-security/2026/10/23/25)\n- [http://www.openwall.com/lists/oss-security/2026/10/24/6](http://www.openwall.com/lists/oss-security/2026/10/24/6)\n- [http://www.openwall.com/lists/oss-security/2026/10/26/12](http://www.openwall.com/lists/oss-security/2026/10/26/12)\n- [http://www.openwall.com/lists/oss-security/2026/10/26/13](http://www.openwall.com/lists/oss-security/2026/10/26/13)\n- [http://www.openwall.com/lists/oss-security/2026/10/26/16](http://www.openwall.com/lists/oss-security/2026/10/26/16)\n- [https://broccoli2shell.com](https://broccoli2shell.com)\n- [https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-9v8h-qqgm-4m35](https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-9v8h-qqgm-4m35)\n- [https://github.com/dotnet/announcements/issues/494](https://github.com/dotnet/announcements/issues/494)\n- [https://github.com/google/brotli/releases/tag/v1.0.10](https://github.com/google/brotli/releases/tag/v1.0.10)\n- [https://github.com/google/brotli/releases/tag/v1.1.1](https://github.com/google/brotli/releases/tag/v1.1.1)\n- [https://github.com/google/brotli/releases/tag/v1.2.1](https://github.com/google/brotli/releases/tag/v1.2.1)\n- [https://lists.debian.org/debian-lts-announce/2026/10/msg00049.html](https://lists.debian.org/debian-lts-announce/2026/10/msg00049.html)\n- [https://patchtheplanet.org/brotli](https://patchtheplanet.org/brotli)\n- [https://www.aikido.dev/blog/node2shell-nodejs-brotli-rce-cve-2026-111497](https://www.aikido.dev/blog/node2shell-nodejs-brotli-rce-cve-2026-111497)\n- [https://ellio.tech/en/blog/node2shell-cve-2026-111497-rce-on-stock-nodejs-builds/](https://ellio.tech/en/blog/node2shell-cve-2026-111497-rce-on-stock-nodejs-builds/)\n- [https://www.cisa.gov/known-exploited-vulnerabilities-catalog?field_cve=CVE-2026-111497](https://www.cisa.gov/known-exploited-vulnerabilities-catalog?field_cve=CVE-2026-111497)\n- [https://github.com/assetnote/node2shell-scanner](https://github.com/assetnote/node2shell-scanner)\n- [https://github.com/projectdiscovery/nuclei-templates/blob/main/http/javascript/cves/2026/CVE-2026-111497.yaml](https://github.com/projectdiscovery/nuclei-templates/blob/main/http/javascript/cves/2026/CVE-2026-111497.yaml)\n- [https://www.cisa.gov/known-exploited-vulnerabilities-catalog](https://www.cisa.gov/known-exploited-vulnerabilities-catalog)\n"
              },
