                "text": "High severity - CRLF Injection vulnerability in io.micrometer:micrometer-core"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "(CVE-2026-59296) io.micrometer:micrometer-core@1.12.5"
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "",
                "markdown": "## Overview\n\nAffected versions of this package are vulnerable to CRLF Injection through `DatadogStatsdLineBuilder`, `EtsyStatsdLineBuilder`, and the `Printer` in `LoggingMeterRegistry`. An attacker can spoof metrics or log entries by supplying meter names, tag keys, or tag values containing `\\n` or `\\r`, causing the generated StatsD or log output to break into additional lines.\r\n\r\n**Notes**\r\n\r\n- Additional fixes are available for earlier versions under Enterprise Support (see the Spring Security Advisory for additional details)\n## Remediation\nUpgrade `io.micrometer:micrometer-core` to version 1.16.7, 1.17.1 or higher.\n## References\n- [GitHub Commit](https://github.com/micrometer-metrics/micrometer/commit/21095149cbb82b914bd9c0688a1622a4a3220f85)\n- [Spring Security Advisory](https://spring.io/security/cve-2026-59296)\n"
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "properties": {
                "tags": [
                  "security",
                  "CWE-93",
                  "maven"
                ],
                "cvssv3_baseScore": 8.2,
                "security-severity": "8.2"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "SNYK-JAVA-IOMICROMETER-19256585",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "High severity - Missing Release of Memory after Effective Lifetime vulnerability in io.micrometer:micrometer-core"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "(CVE-2026-59295) io.micrometer:micrometer-core@1.12.5"
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "",
                "markdown": "## Overview\n\nAffected versions of this package are vulnerable to Missing Release of Memory after Effective Lifetime via the `MicrometerHttpClientInterceptor`. An attacker can cause unbounded memory consumption by repeatedly triggering asynchronous request failures before receiving a response, such as through connection resets or timeouts. This can ultimately lead to heap exhaustion and application crashes.\n## Remediation\nUpgrade `io.micrometer:micrometer-core` to version 1.16.7, 1.17.1 or higher.\n## References\n- [Spring Security Advisory](https://spring.io/security/cve-2026-59295)\n"
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "properties": {
                "tags": [
                  "security",
                  "CWE-401",
                  "maven"
                ],
                "cvssv3_baseScore": 8.2,
                "security-severity": "8.2"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "SNYK-JAVA-ORGAPACHELOGGINGLOG4J-17954276",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Medium severity - Improper Encoding or Escaping of Output vulnerability in org.apache.logging.log4j:log4j-api"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "(CVE-2026-49844) org.apache.logging.log4j:log4j-api@2.21.1"
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "",
                "markdown": "## Overview\n\nAffected versions of this package are vulnerable to Improper Encoding or Escaping of Output in the `MapMessage.asJson()` method, which emits the bare `NaN`, `Infinity`, or `-Infinity` tokens instead of an RFC 8259-compliant representation. An attacker can emit malformed JSON that corrupts the enclosing log record or disrupts downstream log ingestion and parsing by supplying non-finite floating-point values that the application records in a logged `MapMessage`. Exploitation requires the application to use the `message` resolver of `JsonTemplateLayout`, or another layout relying on `MapMessage.asJson()`, and to log a `MapMessage` holding attacker-controlled floating-point values.\n\n**Note:** This is a bypass of the fix for the vulnerability described in [CVE-2026-34481](https://security.snyk.io/vuln/SNYK-JAVA-ORGAPACHELOGGINGLOG4J-15967756).\n## Remediation\nA fix was pushed into the `master` branch but not yet published.\n## References\n- [event-template-resolver-message Documentation](https://logging.apache.org/log4j/2.x/manual/json-template-layout.html#event-template-resolver-message)\n- [GitHub Commit](https://github.com/apache/logging-log4j2/commit/19edb23e162d6c728a8c2221a240037d389ed300)\n- [GitHub PR](https://github.com/apache/logging-log4j2/pull/4163)\n- [Vulnerability Advisory](https://logging.apache.org/security.html#CVE-2026-49844)\n"
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "properties": {
                "tags": [
                  "security",
                  "CWE-116",
                  "maven"
                ],
                "cvssv3_baseScore": 6.3,
                "security-severity": "6.3"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "SNYK-JAVA-ORGAPACHETOMCATEMBED-10264469",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Medium severity - Improper Handling of Case Sensitivity vulnerability in org.apache.tomcat.embed:tomcat-embed-core"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "(CVE-2025-46701) org.apache.tomcat.embed:tomcat-embed-core@10.1.20"
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "",
                "markdown": "## Overview\n[org.apache.tomcat.embed:tomcat-embed-core](https://mvnrepository.com/artifact/org.apache.tomcat.embed/tomcat-embed-core) is a Core Tomcat implementation.\n\nAffected versions of this package are vulnerable to Improper Handling of Case Sensitivity in the `pathInfo` component of a URI mapped to the CGI servlet. An attacker can bypass security constraints that apply to the `pathInfo` component by exploiting this vulnerability on a case insensitive file system.\n## Remediation\nUpgrade `org.apache.tomcat.embed:tomcat-embed-core` to version 9.0.105, 10.1.41, 11.0.7 or higher.\n## References\n- [Apache Advisory](https://lists.apache.org/thread/xhqqk9w5q45srcdqhogdk04lhdscv30j)\n- [Apache Tomcat Advisory](https://tomcat.apache.org/security-10.html#Fixed_in_Apache_Tomcat_10.1.41)\n- [Apache Tomcat Advisory](https://tomcat.apache.org/security-11.html#Fixed_in_Apache_Tomcat_11.0.7)\n- [Apache Tomcat Advisory](https://tomcat.apache.org/security-9.html#Fixed_in_Apache_Tomcat_9.0.105)\n- [GitHub Commit](https://github.com/apache/tomcat/commit/0f01966eb60015d975525019e12a087f05ebf01a)\n- [GitHub Commit](https://github.com/apache/tomcat/commit/238d2aa54b99f91d1111467e2237d2244c64e558)\n- [GitHub Commit](https://github.com/apache/tomcat/commit/2c6800111e7d8d8d5403c07978ea9bff3db5a5a5)\n- [GitHub Commit](https://github.com/apache/tomcat/commit/8cb95ff03221067c511b3fa66d4f745bc4b0a605)\n- [GitHub Commit](https://github.com/apache/tomcat/commit/8df00018a252baa9497615d6420fb6c10466fa74)\n- [GitHub Commit](https://github.com/apache/tomcat/commit/fab7247d2f0e3a29d5daef565f829f383e10e5e2)\n"
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "properties": {
                "tags": [
                  "security",
                  "CWE-178",
                  "maven"
                ],
                "cvssv3_baseScore": 6.3,
                "security-severity": "6.3"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "SNYK-JAVA-ORGAPACHETOMCATEMBED-10365122",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "High severity - Allocation of Resources Without Limits or Throttling vulnerability in org.apache.tomcat.embed:tomcat-embed-core"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "(CVE-2025-48988) org.apache.tomcat.embed:tomcat-embed-core@10.1.20"
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "",
                "markdown": "## Overview\n[org.apache.tomcat.embed:tomcat-embed-core](https://mvnrepository.com/artifact/org.apache.tomcat.embed/tomcat-embed-core) is a Core Tomcat implementation.\n\nAffected versions of this package are vulnerable to Allocation of Resources Without Limits or Throttling due to the uniform handling of request parameters and parts in multipart requests. An attacker can craft a malicious request with a large number of parts, which can lead to a Denial of Service.\n## Remediation\nUpgrade `org.apache.tomcat.embed:tomcat-embed-core` to version 9.0.106, 10.1.42, 11.0.8 or higher.\n## References\n- [Apache Tomcat Advisory](https://tomcat.apache.org/security-10.html)\n- [Apache Tomcat Advisory](https://tomcat.apache.org/security-11.html)\n- [Apache Tomcat Advisory](https://tomcat.apache.org/security-9.html)\n- [Apache Tomcat Thread](https://lists.apache.org/thread/nzkqsok8t42qofgqfmck536mtyzygp18)\n- [GitHub Commit](https://github.com/apache/tomcat/commit/2b0ab14fb55d4edc896e5f1817f2ab76f714ae5e)\n- [GitHub Commit](https://github.com/apache/tomcat/commit/cdde8e655bc1c5c60a07efd216251d77c52fd7f6)\n- [GitHub Commit](https://github.com/apache/tomcat/commit/ee8042ffce4cb9324dfd79efda5984f37bbb6910)\n"
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
