            {
              "id": "SNYK-JAVA-ORGAPACHETOMCATEMBED-13723930",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Medium severity - Improper Resource Shutdown or Release vulnerability in org.apache.tomcat.embed:tomcat-embed-core"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "(CVE-2025-61795) org.apache.tomcat.embed:tomcat-embed-core@10.1.20"
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "",
                "markdown": "## Overview\n[org.apache.tomcat.embed:tomcat-embed-core](https://mvnrepository.com/artifact/org.apache.tomcat.embed/tomcat-embed-core) is a Core Tomcat implementation.\n\nAffected versions of this package are vulnerable to Improper Resource Shutdown or Release due to the delayed cleaning of multipart upload temporary files. An attacker can cause a denial-of-service by sending crafted requests that create temporary copies of uploaded parts faster than the garbage collector clears them, leading to resource exhaustion.\r\n\r\n**Note:** Successful exploitation depends on the JVM settings, the application memory usage, and application load.\n\n## Details\n\nDenial of Service (DoS) describes a family of attacks, all aimed at making a system inaccessible to its intended and legitimate users.\n\nUnlike other vulnerabilities, DoS attacks usually do not aim at breaching security. Rather, they are focused on making websites and services unavailable to genuine users resulting in downtime.\n\nOne popular Denial of Service vulnerability is DDoS (a Distributed Denial of Service), an attack that attempts to clog network pipes to the system by generating a large volume of traffic from many machines.\n\nWhen it comes to open source libraries, DoS vulnerabilities allow attackers to trigger such a crash or crippling of the service by using a flaw either in the application code or from the use of open source libraries.\n\nTwo common types of DoS vulnerabilities:\n\n* High CPU/Memory Consumption- An attacker sending crafted requests that could cause the system to take a disproportionate amount of time to process. For example, [commons-fileupload:commons-fileupload](https://security.snyk.io/vuln/SNYK-JAVA-COMMONSFILEUPLOAD-30082).\n\n* Crash - An attacker sending crafted requests that could cause the system to crash. For Example,  [npm `ws` package](https://snyk.io/vuln/npm:ws:20171108)\n\n## Remediation\nUpgrade `org.apache.tomcat.embed:tomcat-embed-core` to version 9.0.110, 10.1.47, 11.0.12 or higher.\n## References\n- [Apache Mail](https://lists.apache.org/thread/wm9mx8brmx9g4zpywm06ryrtvd3160pp)\n- [GitHub Commit](https://github.com/apache/tomcat/commit/1cdf5f730ede75a0759492f179ac21ca4ff68e06)\n- [GitHub Commit](https://github.com/apache/tomcat/commit/af6e9181620304c0d818121c29c074e1330610d0)\n- [GitHub Commit](https://github.com/apache/tomcat/commit/afa422bd7ca1eef0f507259c682fd876494d9c3b)\n- [Red Hat Bugzilla Bug](https://bugzilla.redhat.com/show_bug.cgi?id=2406588)\n- [Vulnerability Advisory](https://tomcat.apache.org/security-11.html#Fixed_in_Apache_Tomcat_11.0.12)\n"
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "properties": {
                "tags": [
                  "security",
                  "CWE-404",
                  "maven"
                ],
                "cvssv3_baseScore": 6,
                "security-severity": "6"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "SNYK-JAVA-ORGAPACHETOMCATEMBED-13733966",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "High severity - Relative Path Traversal vulnerability in org.apache.tomcat.embed:tomcat-embed-core"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "(CVE-2025-55752) org.apache.tomcat.embed:tomcat-embed-core@10.1.20"
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "",
                "markdown": "## Overview\n[org.apache.tomcat.embed:tomcat-embed-core](https://mvnrepository.com/artifact/org.apache.tomcat.embed/tomcat-embed-core) is a Core Tomcat implementation.\n\nAffected versions of this package are vulnerable to Relative Path Traversal via the URL normalization. An attacker can bypass security constraints and access restricted directories such as `/WEB-INF/` and `/META-INF/` by manipulating the request URI. If PUT requests are also enabled then malicious files could be uploaded leading to remote code execution.\r\n\r\n**Note:**\r\n\r\n1) Older, EOL versions may also be affected.\r\n2) PUT requests are normally limited to trusted users and it is considered unlikely that PUT requests would be enabled in conjunction with a rewrite that manipulated the URI.\n## Remediation\nUpgrade `org.apache.tomcat.embed:tomcat-embed-core` to version 9.0.109, 10.1.45, 11.0.11 or higher.\n## References\n- [Apache Mailing List](https://lists.apache.org/thread/n05kjcwyj1s45ovs8ll1qrrojhfb1tog)\n- [Apache Tomcat Advisory](https://tomcat.apache.org/security-10.html#Fixed_in_Apache_Tomcat_10.1.45)\n- [Apache Tomcat Advisory](https://tomcat.apache.org/security-11.html#Fixed_in_Apache_Tomcat_11.0.11)\n- [Apache Tomcat Advisory](https://tomcat.apache.org/security-9.html#Fixed_in_Apache_Tomcat_9.0.109)\n- [GitHub Commit](https://github.com/apache/tomcat/commit/130d36d8492ef9e4eb22952c17c92423cb35fd06)\n- [GitHub Commit](https://github.com/apache/tomcat/commit/b5042622b8b78340ae65403c55dcb9c7416924df)\n- [GitHub Commit](https://github.com/apache/tomcat/commit/fec06c610ed7466b401e29cc567a58aee5ed826a)\n- [PoC in GitHub](https://github.com/TAM-K592/CVE-2025-55752)\n"
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "properties": {
                "tags": [
                  "security",
                  "CWE-23",
                  "maven"
                ],
                "cvssv3_baseScore": 7.7,
                "security-severity": "7.7"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "SNYK-JAVA-ORGAPACHETOMCATEMBED-13746602",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "High severity - Untrusted Search Path vulnerability in org.apache.tomcat.embed:tomcat-embed-core"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "(CVE-2025-49124) org.apache.tomcat.embed:tomcat-embed-core@10.1.20"
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "",
                "markdown": "## Overview\n[org.apache.tomcat.embed:tomcat-embed-core](https://mvnrepository.com/artifact/org.apache.tomcat.embed/tomcat-embed-core) is a Core Tomcat implementation.\n\nAffected versions of this package are vulnerable to Untrusted Search Path via the `icacls.exe` call during Windows installation, when a full path is not specified. An attacker can execute arbitrary code with elevated privileges by placing a malicious executable in a directory that is searched before the intended system directory.\n## Remediation\nUpgrade `org.apache.tomcat.embed:tomcat-embed-core` to version 9.0.106, 10.1.42, 11.0.8 or higher.\n## References\n- [Apache Advisory](https://lists.apache.org/thread/lnow7tt2j6hb9kcpkggx32ht6o90vqzv)\n- [Apache Tomcat Advisory](https://tomcat.apache.org/security-10.html#Fixed_in_Apache_Tomcat_10.1.42)\n- [Apache Tomcat Advisory](https://tomcat.apache.org/security-11.html#Fixed_in_Apache_Tomcat_11.0.8)\n- [Apache Tomcat Advisory](https://tomcat.apache.org/security-9.html#Fixed_in_Apache_Tomcat_9.0.106)\n- [GitHub Commit](https://github.com/apache/tomcat/commit/c56456cda8151c9504dfb7985700824559d769a7)\n- [GitHub Commit](https://github.com/apache/tomcat/commit/e0e07812224d327a321babb554f5a5758d30cc49)\n- [OSS Security Advisory](http://www.openwall.com/lists/oss-security/2025/06/16/3)\n"
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "properties": {
                "tags": [
                  "security",
                  "CWE-426",
                  "maven"
                ],
                "cvssv3_baseScore": 7.5,
                "security-severity": "7.5"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "SNYK-JAVA-ORGAPACHETOMCATEMBED-15307781",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Critical severity - Improper Certificate Validation vulnerability in org.apache.tomcat.embed:tomcat-embed-core"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "(CVE-2025-66614) org.apache.tomcat.embed:tomcat-embed-core@10.1.20"
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "",
                "markdown": "## Overview\n[org.apache.tomcat.embed:tomcat-embed-core](https://mvnrepository.com/artifact/org.apache.tomcat.embed/tomcat-embed-core) is a Core Tomcat implementation.\n\nAffected versions of this package are vulnerable to Improper Certificate Validation in the SNI extension, when client certificate authentication relies exclusively on the Connector (and is not enforced in the web application). The hostname provided via the SNI extension may be different from the hostname in the HTTP host header field.\n## Remediation\nUpgrade `org.apache.tomcat.embed:tomcat-embed-core` to version 9.0.113, 10.1.50, 11.0.15 or higher.\n## References\n- [Apache Mailing List](https://lists.apache.org/thread/vw6lxtlh2qbqwpb61wd3sv1flm2nttw7)\n- [GitHub Commit](https://github.com/apache/tomcat/commit/258a591b61f8cf5c22109e21e5a2a38b63454fd2)\n"
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "properties": {
                "tags": [
                  "security",
                  "CWE-295",
                  "maven"
                ],
                "cvssv3_baseScore": 9.1,
                "security-severity": "9.1"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "SNYK-JAVA-ORGAPACHETOMCATEMBED-15307822",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "High severity - Incorrect Authorization vulnerability in org.apache.tomcat.embed:tomcat-embed-core"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "(CVE-2026-24734) org.apache.tomcat.embed:tomcat-embed-core@10.1.20"
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "",
                "markdown": "## Overview\n[org.apache.tomcat.embed:tomcat-embed-core](https://mvnrepository.com/artifact/org.apache.tomcat.embed/tomcat-embed-core) is a Core Tomcat implementation.\n\nAffected versions of this package are vulnerable to Incorrect Authorization when using an OCSP responder. OCSP response verification and freshness checks can be bypassed, allowing certificate revocation to be bypassed.\n## Remediation\nUpgrade `org.apache.tomcat.embed:tomcat-embed-core` to version 9.0.114, 10.1.52, 11.0.18 or higher.\n## References\n- [Apache Mailing List](https://lists.apache.org/thread/292dlmx3fz1888v6v16221kpozq56gml)\n- [GitHub Commit](https://github.com/apache/tomcat/commit/e76e9eaa246f30debd603726d9147a8a8cb5171c)\n- [GitHub Commit](https://github.com/apache/tomcat-native/commit/69a977dd427ad2a6da0f10aca3872386ee27f681)\n"
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "properties": {
                "tags": [
                  "security",
                  "CWE-863",
                  "maven"
                ],
                "cvssv3_baseScore": 8.7,
                "security-severity": "8.7"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "SNYK-JAVA-ORGAPACHETOMCATEMBED-15307825",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Low severity - Improper Authorization vulnerability in org.apache.tomcat.embed:tomcat-embed-core"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "(CVE-2026-24733) org.apache.tomcat.embed:tomcat-embed-core@10.1.20"
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "",
                "markdown": "## Overview\n[org.apache.tomcat.embed:tomcat-embed-core](https://mvnrepository.com/artifact/org.apache.tomcat.embed/tomcat-embed-core) is a Core Tomcat implementation.\n\nAffected versions of this package are vulnerable to Improper Authorization in `prepareRequestProtocol()`, which accepts HTTP/0.9 requests other than `GET`. A security constraint configured to allow `HEAD` requests to a URI but deny `GET` requests allows a user to bypass the constraint by sending an invalid `HEAD` request.\n## Remediation\nUpgrade `org.apache.tomcat.embed:tomcat-embed-core` to version 9.0.113, 10.1.50, 11.0.15 or higher.\n## References\n- [Apache Mailing List](https://lists.apache.org/thread/6xk3t65qpn1myp618krtfotbjn1qt90f)\n- [GitHub Commit](https://github.com/apache/tomcat/commit/6c73d74ff281260d74c836370ff6b82f1da8048b)\n"
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "properties": {
                "tags": [
                  "security",
                  "CWE-285",
                  "maven"
                ],
                "cvssv3_baseScore": 2.3,
                "security-severity": "2.3"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "SNYK-JAVA-ORGAPACHETOMCATEMBED-15989808",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "High severity - Improper Authentication vulnerability in org.apache.tomcat.embed:tomcat-embed-core"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "(CVE-2026-29145) org.apache.tomcat.embed:tomcat-embed-core@10.1.20"
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "",
                "markdown": "## Overview\n[org.apache.tomcat.embed:tomcat-embed-core](https://mvnrepository.com/artifact/org.apache.tomcat.embed/tomcat-embed-core) is a Core Tomcat implementation.\n\nAffected versions of this package are vulnerable to Improper Authentication in `processOCSPRequest()`, which is part of the the `CLIENT_CERT` authentication process. An attacker can trigger a soft-fail of OCSP checks when soft-fail is disabled.\n## Remediation\nUpgrade `org.apache.tomcat.embed:tomcat-embed-core` to version 9.0.116, 10.1.53, 11.0.20 or higher.\n## References\n- [Apache Mailing List](https://lists.apache.org/thread/yz5fxmhd2j43wgqykssdo7kltws57jfz)\n- [GitHub Commit](https://github.com/apache/tomcat/commit/721591f7bff424c693f26adc18ae9b9abac3655b)\n- [GitHub Commit](https://github.com/apache/tomcat-native/commit/a0127f7d3b68dca553261f8d7d3540bfeeafc0d2)\n- [OSS Security Advisory](http://www.openwall.com/lists/oss-security/2026/04/09/23)\n"
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "properties": {
                "tags": [
                  "security",
                  "CWE-287",
                  "maven"
                ],
                "cvssv3_baseScore": 8.8,
                "security-severity": "8.8"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "SNYK-JAVA-ORGAPACHETOMCATEMBED-15989812",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Medium severity - Improper Encoding or Escaping of Output vulnerability in org.apache.tomcat.embed:tomcat-embed-core"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "(CVE-2026-34483) org.apache.tomcat.embed:tomcat-embed-core@10.1.20"
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "",
                "markdown": "## Overview\n[org.apache.tomcat.embed:tomcat-embed-core](https://mvnrepository.com/artifact/org.apache.tomcat.embed/tomcat-embed-core) is a Core Tomcat implementation.\n\nAffected versions of this package are vulnerable to Improper Encoding or Escaping of Output in `JsonAccessLogValve()`, which relies on an unescaped `append()` in generating JSON logs. If non-default values are used for the Connector attributes `relaxedPathChars` or `relaxedQueryChars`, an attacker can inject malicious JSON into logs.\n## Remediation\nUpgrade `org.apache.tomcat.embed:tomcat-embed-core` to version 9.0.117, 10.1.54, 11.0.21 or higher.\n## References\n- [Apache Mailing List](https://lists.apache.org/thread/j1w7304yonlr8vo1tkb5nfs7od1y228b)\n- [GitHub Commit](https://github.com/apache/tomcat/commit/f9ddc24fcfcdfaea4a6953198d8636aca3e957bc)\n- [OSS Security Advisory](http://www.openwall.com/lists/oss-security/2026/04/09/26)\n"
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "properties": {
                "tags": [
                  "security",
                  "CWE-116",
                  "maven"
                ],
                "cvssv3_baseScore": 6.3,
                "security-severity": "6.3"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "SNYK-JAVA-ORGAPACHETOMCATEMBED-15989820",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "High severity - Improper Authentication vulnerability in org.apache.tomcat.embed:tomcat-embed-core"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "(CVE-2026-34500) org.apache.tomcat.embed:tomcat-embed-core@10.1.20"
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "",
                "markdown": "## Overview\n[org.apache.tomcat.embed:tomcat-embed-core](https://mvnrepository.com/artifact/org.apache.tomcat.embed/tomcat-embed-core) is a Core Tomcat implementation.\n\nAffected versions of this package are vulnerable to Improper Authentication in `processOCSPRequest()`, which is part of the the `CLIENT_CERT` authentication process. In some \"edge cases\", an attacker can trigger a soft-fail of OCSP checks when soft-fail is disabled.\n## Remediation\nUpgrade `org.apache.tomcat.embed:tomcat-embed-core` to version 9.0.117, 10.1.54, 11.0.21 or higher.\n## References\n- [Apache Mailing List](https://lists.apache.org/thread/7rcl4zdxryc8hy3htyfyxkbqpxjtfdl2)\n- [GitHub Commit](https://github.com/apache/tomcat/commit/c13e60e732ea6d07087293a41ad1866c20848271)\n- [OSS Security Advisory](http://www.openwall.com/lists/oss-security/2026/04/09/29)\n"
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
