            {
              "id": "SNYK-JAVA-ORGAPACHETOMCATEMBED-20302843",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Critical severity - Incorrect Authorization vulnerability in org.apache.tomcat.embed:tomcat-embed-core"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "(CVE-2026-68525) org.apache.tomcat.embed:tomcat-embed-core@10.1.20"
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "",
                "markdown": "## Overview\n[org.apache.tomcat.embed:tomcat-embed-core](https://mvnrepository.com/artifact/org.apache.tomcat.embed/tomcat-embed-core) is a Core Tomcat implementation.\n\nAffected versions of this package are vulnerable to Incorrect Authorization via the `FormAuthenticator` and `AuthenticatorBase` FORM authentication flow. An attacker can bypass a security constraint that allows access to a resource for `POST` but not `GET` by authenticating through FORM login and restoring a saved request with a different HTTP method. This lets a request that should be blocked reach the protected resource, exposing content or actions that the user should not be allowed to access with that method.\r\n\r\n**Notes**\r\n\r\n- The issue was fixed in Apache Tomcat 10.1.58, but the release vote for the 10.1.58 release candidate did not pass. Therefore, although users must download 10.1.59 to obtain a version that includes a fix for this issue, version 10.1.58 is not included in the list of affected versions.\n## Remediation\nUpgrade `org.apache.tomcat.embed:tomcat-embed-core` to version 9.0.121, 10.1.58, 11.0.25 or higher.\n## References\n- [Apache Security Advisory](https://lists.apache.org/thread/x1y2lfsgzxwzc456f8954vbvgn03zhd7)\n- [GitHub Commit 10.1.58](https://github.com/apache/tomcat/commit/58123aa468a20e2a079b7e0c68a4009e2475c098)\n- [GitHub Commit 11.0.25](https://github.com/apache/tomcat/commit/10d048e16034ddf12055e0cede0da05b15c823b8)\n- [GitHub Commit 9.0.121](https://github.com/apache/tomcat/commit/32f0c38526b4e655ff0c17cd97afedefc624fe43)\n"
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "properties": {
                "tags": [
                  "security",
                  "CWE-863",
                  "maven"
                ],
                "cvssv3_baseScore": 9.3,
                "security-severity": "9.3"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "SNYK-JAVA-ORGAPACHETOMCATEMBED-20302874",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Medium severity - Insufficient Session Expiration vulnerability in org.apache.tomcat.embed:tomcat-embed-core"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "(CVE-2026-73180) org.apache.tomcat.embed:tomcat-embed-core@10.1.20"
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "",
                "markdown": "## Overview\n[org.apache.tomcat.embed:tomcat-embed-core](https://mvnrepository.com/artifact/org.apache.tomcat.embed/tomcat-embed-core) is a Core Tomcat implementation.\n\nAffected versions of this package are vulnerable to Insufficient Session Expiration due to the improper termination of WebSocket sessions when the associated HTTP session ends. An attacker can maintain access to resources beyond the intended session duration by establishing a WebSocket connection under an authenticated HTTP session and continuing to interact through the WebSocket after the HTTP session has expired.\r\n\r\n**Note:** This issue was fixed in Apache Tomcat 10.1.58 but the release vote for the 10.1.58 release candidate did not pass. Therefore, although users must download 10.1.59 to obtain a version that includes a fix for this issue, version 10.1.58 is not included in the list of affected versions.\n## Remediation\nUpgrade `org.apache.tomcat.embed:tomcat-embed-core` to version 9.0.121, 10.1.59, 11.0.25 or higher.\n## References\n- [Apache Mailing List](https://lists.apache.org/thread/3j15vztszpyqss253mjq5v1kp7s6hooq)\n- [GitHub Commit](https://github.com/apache/tomcat/commit/e617a5d483b78851d289ca8dc1d68c49b541b419)\n"
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "properties": {
                "tags": [
                  "security",
                  "CWE-613",
                  "maven"
                ],
                "cvssv3_baseScore": 5.3,
                "security-severity": "5.3"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "SNYK-JAVA-ORGAPACHETOMCATEMBED-20302889",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "High severity - Authentication Bypass by Primary Weakness vulnerability in org.apache.tomcat.embed:tomcat-embed-core"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "(CVE-2026-68569) org.apache.tomcat.embed:tomcat-embed-core@10.1.20"
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "",
                "markdown": "## Overview\n[org.apache.tomcat.embed:tomcat-embed-core](https://mvnrepository.com/artifact/org.apache.tomcat.embed/tomcat-embed-core) is a Core Tomcat implementation.\n\nAffected versions of this package are vulnerable to Authentication Bypass by Primary Weakness in the authentication process when using certain authentication mechanisms such as `CLIENT-CERT` or `SPNEGO`. An attacker can gain unauthorized access by authenticating with credentials that do not correspond to a valid user in the `DataSourceRealm`.\r\n\r\n**Note:** This issue was fixed in Apache Tomcat 10.1.58 but the release vote for the 10.1.58 release candidate did not pass. Therefore, although users must download 10.1.59 to obtain a version that includes a fix for this issue, version 10.1.58 is not included in the list of affected versions.\n## Remediation\nUpgrade `org.apache.tomcat.embed:tomcat-embed-core` to version 9.0.121, 10.1.59, 11.0.25 or higher.\n## References\n- [Apache Mailing List](https://lists.apache.org/thread/8robqo76q0osxgw0b5lcwgz0hcf9h4zc)\n- [GitHub Commit](https://github.com/apache/tomcat/commit/790d6e2c3b4cd201a1fa556a23d5b7504dee18ad)\n"
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "properties": {
                "tags": [
                  "security",
                  "CWE-305",
                  "maven"
                ],
                "cvssv3_baseScore": 8.7,
                "security-severity": "8.7"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "SNYK-JAVA-ORGAPACHETOMCATEMBED-20304748",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "High severity - Allocation of Resources Without Limits or Throttling vulnerability in org.apache.tomcat.embed:tomcat-embed-core"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "(CVE-2026-68763) org.apache.tomcat.embed:tomcat-embed-core@10.1.20"
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "",
                "markdown": "## Overview\n[org.apache.tomcat.embed:tomcat-embed-core](https://mvnrepository.com/artifact/org.apache.tomcat.embed/tomcat-embed-core) is a Core Tomcat implementation.\n\nAffected versions of this package are vulnerable to Allocation of Resources Without Limits or Throttling in the HTTP/2 backlog tracking when a stream is reset. An attacker can exhaust system resources by repeatedly resetting streams, leading to service disruption.\r\n\r\n**Note:** This issue was fixed in Apache Tomcat 10.1.58 but the release vote for the 10.1.58 release candidate did not pass. Therefore, although users must download 10.1.59 to obtain a version that includes a fix for this issue, version 10.1.58 is not included in the list of affected versions.\n## Remediation\nUpgrade `org.apache.tomcat.embed:tomcat-embed-core` to version 9.0.121, 10.1.59, 11.0.25 or higher.\n## References\n- [Apache Mailing List](https://lists.apache.org/thread/tv51ty39ppv41v04hdtkp9dp7tg02nzl)\n- [GitHub Commit](https://github.com/apache/tomcat/commit/2a5ec806971627943db18601203129d9c58d959f)\n"
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "properties": {
