                  "security",
                  "CWE-770",
                  "maven"
                ],
                "cvssv3_baseScore": 8.7,
                "security-severity": "8.7"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "SNYK-JAVA-ORGAPACHETOMCATEMBED-21249727",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Medium severity - Incorrect Authorization vulnerability in org.apache.tomcat.embed:tomcat-embed-core"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "(CVE-2026-65182) org.apache.tomcat.embed:tomcat-embed-core@10.1.20"
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "",
                "markdown": "## Overview\n[org.apache.tomcat.embed:tomcat-embed-core](https://mvnrepository.com/artifact/org.apache.tomcat.embed/tomcat-embed-core) is a Core Tomcat implementation.\n\nAffected versions of this package are vulnerable to Incorrect Authorization in the processing of security constraints when a constraint for a longer path is specified before a more restrictive constraint for a shorter sub-path. An attacker can gain unauthorized access to protected resources by crafting requests that exploit the order of security constraints.\r\n\r\n**Note:** This issue was fixed in Apache Tomcat 10.1.58 but the release vote for the 10.1.58 release candidate did not pass. Therefore, although users must download 10.1.59 to obtain a version that includes a fix for this issue, version 10.1.58 is not included in the list of affected versions.\n## Remediation\nUpgrade `org.apache.tomcat.embed:tomcat-embed-core` to version 9.0.121, 10.1.59, 11.0.25 or higher.\n## References\n- [Apache Mailing List](https://lists.apache.org/thread/joosxvzc9b49ttj8lj0jw9mqt0ml767m)\n- [GitHub Commit](https://github.com/apache/tomcat/commit/10d048e16034ddf12055e0cede0da05b15c823b8)\n"
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "properties": {
