            {
              "id": "SNYK-JAVA-ORGAPACHETOMCATEMBED-21715432",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Low severity - Improper Check for Certificate Revocation vulnerability in org.apache.tomcat.embed:tomcat-embed-core"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "(CVE-2026-73581) org.apache.tomcat.embed:tomcat-embed-core@10.1.20"
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "",
                "markdown": "## Overview\n[org.apache.tomcat.embed:tomcat-embed-core](https://mvnrepository.com/artifact/org.apache.tomcat.embed/tomcat-embed-core) is a Core Tomcat implementation.\n\nAffected versions of this package are vulnerable to Improper Check for Certificate Revocation via the `OpenSSLContext` implementations in its OpenSSL and OpenSSL-FFM TLS components. When OpenSSL trust is used and the server key is held in a Java keystore, these implementations ignore configured CRLs; an attacker can present a revoked client certificate during TLS authentication and be treated as a valid user, gaining access to resources protected by client-certificate authentication.\n## Remediation\nUpgrade `org.apache.tomcat.embed:tomcat-embed-core` to version 9.0.122, 10.1.59, 11.0.26 or higher.\n## References\n- [Apache Security Advisory](https://lists.apache.org/thread/r0dj3h1pbn4wv96fhsfrnz3t6874t6do)\n- [GitHub Commit](https://github.com/apache/tomcat/commit/46394cdbbed2cd8446279f347f1f38d19e27a352)\n- [GitHub Commit 10.1.60](https://github.com/apache/tomcat/commit/6907d47ea2d4c3f13ef9f65b0c51ff2fd485c252)\n- [GitHub Commit 11.0.26](https://github.com/apache/tomcat/commit/15a76156ced9f6a6306ef7d6f2e343034231a2de)\n- [GitHub Commit 9.0.122](https://github.com/apache/tomcat/commit/2dce8f26b3ba6a89c8f172b94fa41a5fa2dcc361)\n"
              },
