            {
              "id": "SNYK-JAVA-ORGAPACHETOMCATEMBED-9396739",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "High severity - Path Equivalence vulnerability in org.apache.tomcat.embed:tomcat-embed-core"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "(CVE-2025-24813) org.apache.tomcat.embed:tomcat-embed-core@10.1.20"
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "",
                "markdown": "## Overview\n[org.apache.tomcat.embed:tomcat-embed-core](https://mvnrepository.com/artifact/org.apache.tomcat.embed/tomcat-embed-core) is a Core Tomcat implementation.\n\nAffected versions of this package are vulnerable to Path Equivalence in the `doPut()` function in `DefaultServlet.java`, which insecurely replaces path separators with `.`s. \r\n\r\nIf the Default Servlet is configured with writes enabled - which it is not by default - a user can exploit Tomcat's partial `PUT` functionality to achieve code execution via deserialization. The target URL containing sensitive uploaded files must be a sub-directory of a target URL for public uploads, and the malicious user must know the names of the target sensitive files, which are also uploaded using a partial `PUT`. If both attacker and target application are using the default storage location and it contains a library that deserializes untrusted code, the attacker can trigger the execution of malicious code.\n## Remediation\nUpgrade `org.apache.tomcat.embed:tomcat-embed-core` to version 9.0.99, 10.1.35, 11.0.3 or higher.\n## References\n- [GitHub Commit](https://github.com/apache/tomcat/commit/0a668e0c27f2b7ca0cc7c6eea32253b9b5ecb29c)\n- [GitHub Commit](https://github.com/apache/tomcat/commit/eb61aade8f8daccaecabf07d428b877975622f72)\n- [GitHub Commit](https://github.com/apache/tomcat/commit/f6c01d6577cf9a1e06792be47e623d36acc3b5dc)\n- [OSS Security Advisory](http://www.openwall.com/lists/oss-security/2025/03/10/5)\n- [PoC](https://github.com/iSee857/CVE-2025-24813-PoC/blob/main/Tomcat_CVE-2025-24813_RCE.py)\n- [Nuclei Templates](https://github.com/projectdiscovery/nuclei-templates/blob/main/http/cves/2025/CVE-2025-24813.yaml)\n- [CISA - Known Exploited Vulnerabilities](https://www.cisa.gov/known-exploited-vulnerabilities-catalog)\n- [Exploit DB](https://www.exploit-db.com/exploits/52134)\n- [PoC in GitHub](https://github.com/qzy0x/cve-2025-24813_poc)\n"
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "properties": {
                "tags": [
                  "security",
                  "CWE-44",
                  "maven"
                ],
                "cvssv3_baseScore": 7.7,
                "security-severity": "7.7"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "SNYK-JAVA-ORGAPACHETOMCATEMBED-9905132",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "High severity - Improper Cleanup on Thrown Exception vulnerability in org.apache.tomcat.embed:tomcat-embed-core"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "(CVE-2025-31650) org.apache.tomcat.embed:tomcat-embed-core@10.1.20"
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "",
                "markdown": "## Overview\n[org.apache.tomcat.embed:tomcat-embed-core](https://mvnrepository.com/artifact/org.apache.tomcat.embed/tomcat-embed-core) is a Core Tomcat implementation.\n\nAffected versions of this package are vulnerable to Improper Cleanup on Thrown Exception when handling failed HTTP/2 requests with certain invalid HTTP priority headers. An attacker can trigger an `OutOfMemoryException` by sending a large number of malicious requests.\r\n\r\n**Note:** The project maintainers note that version 9.0.103 also fixes the vulnerability but was never officially released.\n## Remediation\nUpgrade `org.apache.tomcat.embed:tomcat-embed-core` to version 9.0.104, 10.1.40, 11.0.6 or higher.\n## References\n- [Apache Mailing List](https://lists.apache.org/thread/j6zzk0y3yym9pzfzkq5vcyxzz0yzh826)\n- [Apache Tomcat Advisory](https://tomcat.apache.org/security-10.html)\n- [Apache Tomcat Advisory](https://tomcat.apache.org/security-11.html)\n- [Apache Tomcat Advisory](https://tomcat.apache.org/security-9.html)\n- [GitHub Commit](https://github.com/apache/tomcat/commit/1eef1dc459c45f1e421d8bd25ef340fc1cc34edc)\n- [GitHub Commit](https://github.com/apache/tomcat/commit/40ae788c2e64d018b4e58cd4210bb96434d0100d)\n- [GitHub Commit](https://github.com/apache/tomcat/commit/75554da2fc5574862510ae6f0d7b3d78937f1d40)\n- [GitHub Commit](https://github.com/apache/tomcat/commit/8cc3b8fb3f2d8d4d6a757e014f19d1fafa948a60)\n- [GitHub Commit](https://github.com/apache/tomcat/commit/b7674782679e1514a0d154166b1d04d38aaac4a9)\n- [GitHub Commit](https://github.com/apache/tomcat/commit/b98e74f517b36929f4208506e5adad22cb767baa)\n- [GitHub Commit](https://github.com/apache/tomcat/commit/cba1a0fe1289ee7f5dd46c61c38d1e1ac5437bff)\n- [GitHub Commit](https://github.com/apache/tomcat/commit/ded0285b96b4d3f5560dfc8856ad5ec4a9b50ba9)\n- [GitHub Commit](https://github.com/apache/tomcat/commit/f619e6a05029538886d5a9d987925d573b5bb8c2)\n- [OSS Security Advisory](http://www.openwall.com/lists/oss-security/2025/04/28/2)\n- [PoC](https://github.com/nomi-sec/PoC-in-GitHub/tree/master/2025/CVE-2025-31650.json)\n- [Exploit DB](https://www.exploit-db.com/exploits/52318)\n- [PoC in GitHub](https://github.com/absholi7ly/TomcatKiller-CVE-2025-31650)\n"
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "properties": {
                "tags": [
                  "security",
                  "CWE-460",
                  "maven"
                ],
                "cvssv3_baseScore": 8.7,
                "security-severity": "8.7"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "SNYK-JAVA-ORGAPACHETOMCATEMBED-9905136",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Medium severity - Improper Neutralization vulnerability in org.apache.tomcat.embed:tomcat-embed-core"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "(CVE-2025-31651) org.apache.tomcat.embed:tomcat-embed-core@10.1.20"
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "",
                "markdown": "## Overview\n[org.apache.tomcat.embed:tomcat-embed-core](https://mvnrepository.com/artifact/org.apache.tomcat.embed/tomcat-embed-core) is a Core Tomcat implementation.\n\nAffected versions of this package are vulnerable to Improper Neutralization in the `RewriteValve` class, which handles rewrite rules. If rewrite rules are configured to enforce security constraints, those security constraints can be bypassed in some cases by sending a malicious request involving `;` or `?` characters.\r\n\r\n**Note:** The project maintainers note that version 9.0.103 also fixes the vulnerability but was never officially released.\n## Remediation\nUpgrade `org.apache.tomcat.embed:tomcat-embed-core` to version 9.0.104, 10.1.40, 11.0.6 or higher.\n## References\n- [Apache Mailing List](https://lists.apache.org/thread/cpklvqwvdrp4k9hmd2l3q33j0gzy4fox)\n- [Apache Tomcat Advisory](https://tomcat.apache.org/security-10.html)\n- [Apache Tomcat Advisory](https://tomcat.apache.org/security-11.html)\n- [Apache Tomcat Advisory](https://tomcat.apache.org/security-9.html)\n- [GitHub Commit](https://github.com/apache/tomcat/commit/066bf6b6a15a4e7e0941d4acf096841165b97098)\n- [GitHub Commit](https://github.com/apache/tomcat/commit/175dc75fc428930034a6c93fb52f830d955d8e64)\n- [GitHub Commit](https://github.com/apache/tomcat/commit/ee3ab548e92345eca0cbd1f01649eb36c6f29454)\n- [GitHub Commit](https://github.com/apache/tomcat/commit/fbecc915a10c5a3d634c5e2c6ced4ff479ce9953)\n- [OSS Security Advisory](http://www.openwall.com/lists/oss-security/2025/04/28/3)\n- [PoC](https://github.com/nomi-sec/PoC-in-GitHub/tree/master/2025/CVE-2025-31651.json)\n"
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "properties": {
                "tags": [
                  "security",
                  "CWE-150",
                  "maven"
                ],
                "cvssv3_baseScore": 6.3,
                "security-severity": "6.3"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "SNYK-JAVA-ORGAPACHETOMCATEMBED-16643269",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Medium severity - Exposure of Private Personal Information to an Unauthorized Actor vulnerability in org.apache.tomcat.embed:tomcat-embed-websocket"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "(CVE-2026-42498) org.apache.tomcat.embed:tomcat-embed-websocket@10.1.20"
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "",
                "markdown": "## Overview\n\nAffected versions of this package are vulnerable to Exposure of Private Personal Information to an Unauthorized Actor in WebSocket client during authentication. An attacker can obtain sensitive HTTP authentication headers by initiating a WebSocket handshake with a malicious host.\n## Remediation\nUpgrade `org.apache.tomcat.embed:tomcat-embed-websocket` to version 8.0.1, 9.0.0.M1, 9.0.118, 10.1.55, 11.0.22 or higher.\n## References\n- [Apache Mailing List](https://lists.apache.org/thread/n61zwf75jrv09rz90j4jssncm244bwdb)\n- [GitHub Commit](https://github.com/apache/tomcat/commit/b288a7a92d1dfe85c90bb1f485bcbbc66f4de1af)\n- [OSS Security Advisory](https://www.openwall.com/lists/oss-security/2026/05/12/14)\n"
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "properties": {
                "tags": [
                  "security",
                  "CWE-359",
                  "maven"
                ],
                "cvssv3_baseScore": 6.9,
                "security-severity": "6.9"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "SNYK-JAVA-ORGAPACHETOMCATEMBED-20302876",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Medium severity - Insufficient Session Expiration vulnerability in org.apache.tomcat.embed:tomcat-embed-websocket"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "(CVE-2026-73180) org.apache.tomcat.embed:tomcat-embed-websocket@10.1.20"
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "",
                "markdown": "## Overview\n\nAffected versions of this package are vulnerable to Insufficient Session Expiration due to the improper termination of WebSocket sessions when the associated HTTP session ends. An attacker can maintain access to resources beyond the intended session duration by establishing a WebSocket connection under an authenticated HTTP session and continuing to interact through the WebSocket after the HTTP session has expired.\r\n\r\n**Note:** This issue was fixed in Apache Tomcat 10.1.58 but the release vote for the 10.1.58 release candidate did not pass. Therefore, although users must download 10.1.59 to obtain a version that includes a fix for this issue, version 10.1.58 is not included in the list of affected versions.\n## Remediation\nUpgrade `org.apache.tomcat.embed:tomcat-embed-websocket` to version 9.0.121, 10.1.59, 11.0.25 or higher.\n## References\n- [Apache Mailing List](https://lists.apache.org/thread/3j15vztszpyqss253mjq5v1kp7s6hooq)\n- [GitHub Commit](https://github.com/apache/tomcat/commit/e617a5d483b78851d289ca8dc1d68c49b541b419)\n"
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "properties": {
                "tags": [
                  "security",
                  "CWE-613",
                  "maven"
                ],
                "cvssv3_baseScore": 5.3,
                "security-severity": "5.3"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "SNYK-JAVA-ORGAPACHETOMCATEMBED-20552494",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Critical severity - Authentication Bypass by Alternate Name vulnerability in org.apache.tomcat.embed:tomcat-embed-websocket"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "(CVE-2026-76183) org.apache.tomcat.embed:tomcat-embed-websocket@10.1.20"
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "",
                "markdown": "## Overview\n\nAffected versions of this package are vulnerable to Authentication Bypass by Alternate Name via the `WebSocket` endpoint security constraint handling. An attacker can gain unauthorized access to protected resources by connecting to endpoints using alternate names.\n## Remediation\nUpgrade `org.apache.tomcat.embed:tomcat-embed-websocket` to version 9.0.122, 10.1.60, 11.0.26 or higher.\n## References\n- [Apache Mailing List](https://lists.apache.org/thread/45mxk8nj2q8pkhct6lfxkvtm2jpywrsp)\n- [GitHub Commit](https://github.com/apache/tomcat/commit/5b48790abd13d94c2bd351027a39a671916b5ddf)\n- [GitHub Commit](https://github.com/apache/tomcat/commit/a93a60a33f4cc202542eb6a0b87b7142d7db311c)\n- [GitHub Commit](https://github.com/apache/tomcat/commit/fa50a173ff3d8d403828441eb450fe6ec63d0955)\n"
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "properties": {
                "tags": [
                  "security",
                  "CWE-289",
                  "maven"
                ],
                "cvssv3_baseScore": 9.3,
                "security-severity": "9.3"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "SNYK-JAVA-ORGAPACHETOMCATEMBED-21246252",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "High severity - Missing Release of Resource after Effective Lifetime vulnerability in org.apache.tomcat.embed:tomcat-embed-websocket"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "(CVE-2026-79677) org.apache.tomcat.embed:tomcat-embed-websocket@10.1.20"
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "",
                "markdown": "## Overview\n\nAffected versions of this package are vulnerable to Missing Release of Resource after Effective Lifetime through the WebSocket write timeout handling in `org.apache.tomcat.websocket.WsRemoteEndpointImplBase`, `WsRemoteEndpointImplClient`, `WsRemoteEndpointImplServer`, and `MessagePart`. An attacker can keep asynchronous WebSocket sends from timing out by sending message fragments or consecutive writes that reuse the same timeout, causing the timeout state to be lost during write processing. When this happens, the server can keep waiting on stalled WebSocket writes instead of aborting them, tying up resources and eventually preventing the application from serving other requests.\n## Remediation\nUpgrade `org.apache.tomcat.embed:tomcat-embed-websocket` to version 11.0.26, 10.1.60, 9.0.122 or higher.\n## References\n- [Apache Security Advisory](https://lists.apache.org/thread/bzwps6ck4szf2hmksbbon3syyl9qnkv8)\n- [GitHub Commit 10.1.60](https://github.com/apache/tomcat/commit/df2f47fe32c4bd528af8b1db099c6710f34d9d5f)\n- [GitHub Commit 11.0.26](https://github.com/apache/tomcat/commit/39edac61dde6b5cd7f88a1d3a35fa9d93fdc3a3e)\n- [GitHub Commit 9.0.122](https://github.com/apache/tomcat/commit/58fdf6df55d38c7b8b0d02568e3d52b07a9774c3)\n"
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "properties": {
                "tags": [
                  "security",
                  "CWE-772",
                  "maven"
                ],
                "cvssv3_baseScore": 8.7,
                "security-severity": "8.7"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "SNYK-JAVA-ORGAPACHETOMCATEMBED-21249759",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "High severity - Denial of Service (DoS) vulnerability in org.apache.tomcat.embed:tomcat-embed-websocket"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "(CVE-2026-77791) org.apache.tomcat.embed:tomcat-embed-websocket@10.1.20"
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "",
                "markdown": "## Overview\n\nAffected versions of this package are vulnerable to Denial of Service (DoS) via busy wait during WebSocket close.\n\n## Details\n\nDenial of Service (DoS) describes a family of attacks, all aimed at making a system inaccessible to its intended and legitimate users.\n\nUnlike other vulnerabilities, DoS attacks usually do not aim at breaching security. Rather, they are focused on making websites and services unavailable to genuine users resulting in downtime.\n\nOne popular Denial of Service vulnerability is DDoS (a Distributed Denial of Service), an attack that attempts to clog network pipes to the system by generating a large volume of traffic from many machines.\n\nWhen it comes to open source libraries, DoS vulnerabilities allow attackers to trigger such a crash or crippling of the service by using a flaw either in the application code or from the use of open source libraries.\n\nTwo common types of DoS vulnerabilities:\n\n* High CPU/Memory Consumption- An attacker sending crafted requests that could cause the system to take a disproportionate amount of time to process. For example, [commons-fileupload:commons-fileupload](https://security.snyk.io/vuln/SNYK-JAVA-COMMONSFILEUPLOAD-30082).\n\n* Crash - An attacker sending crafted requests that could cause the system to crash. For Example,  [npm `ws` package](https://snyk.io/vuln/npm:ws:20171108)\n\n## Remediation\nUpgrade `org.apache.tomcat.embed:tomcat-embed-websocket` to version 9.0.121, 10.1.59, 11.0.25 or higher.\n## References\n- [Apache Mailing List](https://lists.apache.org/thread/mb1pjjooqytrl6hbvbt3rw1lqwlon4cz)\n- [Apache Tomcat Advisory](https://tomcat.apache.org/security-10.html)\n- [Apache Tomcat Advisory](https://tomcat.apache.org/security-11.html)\n- [Apache Tomcat Advisory](https://tomcat.apache.org/security-9.html)\n- [GitHub Commit](https://github.com/apache/tomcat/commit/7a5945f1de1d3310214234dfbbd7c569af52d058)\n- [GitHub Commit](https://github.com/apache/tomcat/commit/ce291bbc65393e3bfbec2a8d23fcee0106a1ade9)\n- [GitHub Commit](https://github.com/apache/tomcat/commit/e896f73c868f66dfb2a93565fda4d13cd5909d2d)\n"
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "properties": {
                "tags": [
                  "security",
                  "CWE-400",
                  "maven"
                ],
                "cvssv3_baseScore": 8.7,
                "security-severity": "8.7"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "SNYK-JAVA-ORGAPACHETOMCATEMBED-21715428",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Medium severity - Improper Handling of Length Parameter Inconsistency vulnerability in org.apache.tomcat.embed:tomcat-embed-websocket"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "(CVE-2026-87022) org.apache.tomcat.embed:tomcat-embed-websocket@10.1.20"
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "",
                "markdown": "## Overview\n\nAffected versions of this package are vulnerable to Improper Handling of Length Parameter Inconsistency via the `getMoreData` method in the `PerMessageDeflate` transformation. An attacker can send a per-message-deflate payload containing multiple DEFLATE blocks where a block sets `BFINAL` before later blocks; Tomcat may end processing while compressed bytes remain, causing message data to be ignored and allowing message contents to be smuggled. This affects WebSocket connections using per-message-deflate.\n## Remediation\nUpgrade `org.apache.tomcat.embed:tomcat-embed-websocket` to version 9.0.122, 10.1.60, 11.0.26 or higher.\n## References\n- [Apache Mailing List](https://lists.apache.org/thread/ypvlkjqsq0480fnk9jm6h9qllddwlw4w)\n- [GitHub Commit](https://github.com/apache/tomcat/commit/0697b66bd823daa23e91c3e3c63fc4765cebc66d)\n- [GitHub Commit 10.1.60](https://github.com/apache/tomcat/commit/567a85515b78d1cd6410a89844b88109fcc2306f)\n- [GitHub Commit 11.0.26](https://github.com/apache/tomcat/commit/4fef25fe2ab7509e697af093280b9daadb515615)\n- [GitHub Commit 9.0.122](https://github.com/apache/tomcat/commit/959a52a227cc35101b92dae35b722546167594d6)\n"
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "properties": {
                "tags": [
                  "security",
                  "CWE-130",
                  "maven"
                ],
                "cvssv3_baseScore": 6.9,
                "security-severity": "6.9"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "SNYK-JAVA-ORGSPRINGFRAMEWORK-10176071",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Low severity - Improper Handling of Case Sensitivity vulnerability in org.springframework:spring-context"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "(CVE-2025-22233) org.springframework:spring-context@6.1.6"
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "",
                "markdown": "## Overview\n\nAffected versions of this package are vulnerable to Improper Handling of Case Sensitivity due to an incomplete fix for [CVE-2024-38820](https://security.snyk.io/vuln/SNYK-JAVA-ORGSPRINGFRAMEWORK-8230364), where it is still possible to bypass the `disallowedFields` checks.\n\n**Note:**\n\nThis vulnerability was also fixed in commercial versions 6.0.28 and 5.3.43.\n## Remediation\nUpgrade `org.springframework:spring-context` to version 6.1.20, 6.2.7 or higher.\n## References\n- [GitHub Commit](https://github.com/spring-projects/spring-framework/commit/ee62701f5634e904e42e218baad142cea2bcd332)\n- [GitHub Issue](https://github.com/spring-projects/spring-framework/issues/34801)\n- [Spring Security Advisory](https://spring.io/security/cve-2025-22233)\n"
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "properties": {
                "tags": [
                  "security",
                  "CWE-178",
                  "maven"
                ],
                "cvssv3_baseScore": 2.3,
                "security-severity": "2.3"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "SNYK-JAVA-ORGSPRINGFRAMEWORK-8230364",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Low severity - Improper Handling of Case Sensitivity vulnerability in org.springframework:spring-context"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "(CVE-2024-38820) org.springframework:spring-context@6.1.6"
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "",
                "markdown": "## Overview\n\nAffected versions of this package are vulnerable to Improper Handling of Case Sensitivity due to `String.toLowerCase()` having some Locale dependent exceptions that could potentially result in fields not protected as expected.\r\n\r\n**Note:**\r\n\r\nThe fix for [CVE-2022-22968](https://security.snyk.io/vuln/SNYK-JAVA-ORGSPRINGFRAMEWORK-2689634) made `disallowedFields` patterns in `DataBinder` case insensitive.\r\n\r\nThis vulnerability was also fixed in commercial versions 5.3.41 and 6.0.25.\n## Remediation\nUpgrade `org.springframework:spring-context` to version 6.1.14 or higher.\n## References\n- [GitHub Commit](https://github.com/spring-projects/spring-framework/commit/23656aebc6c7d0f9faff1080981eb4d55eff296c)\n- [Spring Security Advisory](https://spring.io/security/cve-2024-38820)\n"
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "properties": {
                "tags": [
                  "security",
                  "CWE-178",
                  "maven"
                ],
                "cvssv3_baseScore": 2.3,
                "security-severity": "2.3"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "SNYK-JAVA-ORGSPRINGFRAMEWORK-10345766",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Medium severity - HTTP Response Splitting vulnerability in org.springframework:spring-web"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "(CVE-2025-41234) org.springframework:spring-web@6.1.6"
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "",
                "markdown": "## Overview\n[org.springframework:spring-web](https://github.com/spring-projects/spring-framework) is a package that provides a comprehensive programming and configuration model for modern Java-based enterprise applications - on any kind of deployment platform.\n\nAffected versions of this package are vulnerable to HTTP Response Splitting via the `Content-Disposition` header where the `filename` parameter value could contain non-printable characters, causing parsing issues for HTTP clients. An attacker can cause the download of files containing malicious commands by injecting content into the response.\n\n**Notes:**\n\n1) This is only exploitable if the header is prepared with `org.springframework.http.ContentDisposition`, the filename is set via `ContentDisposition.Builder#filename(String, Charset)`, the value is derived from unsanitized user input, and the attacker can inject malicious content into the downloaded response.\n\n2) The vulnerability was also fixed in the 6.0.29 commercial version.\n## Remediation\nUpgrade `org.springframework:spring-web` to version 6.1.21, 6.2.8 or higher.\n## References\n- [GitHub Commit](https://github.com/spring-projects/spring-framework/commit/f0e7b42704e6b33958f242d91bd690d6ef7ada9c)\n- [GitHub Issue](https://github.com/spring-projects/spring-framework/issues/35034)\n- [Spring Security Advisory](https://spring.io/security/cve-2025-41234)\n"
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "properties": {
                "tags": [
                  "security",
                  "CWE-113",
                  "maven"
                ],
                "cvssv3_baseScore": 4.5,
                "security-severity": "4.5"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "SNYK-JAVA-ORGSPRINGFRAMEWORK-15701755",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Low severity - Improper Neutralization of Special Elements in Output Used by a Downstream Component ('Injection') vulnerability in org.springframework:spring-web"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "(CVE-2026-22735) org.springframework:spring-web@6.1.6"
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "",
                "markdown": "## Overview\n[org.springframework:spring-web](https://github.com/spring-projects/spring-framework) is a package that provides a comprehensive programming and configuration model for modern Java-based enterprise applications - on any kind of deployment platform.\n\nAffected versions of this package are vulnerable to Improper Neutralization of Special Elements in Output Used by a Downstream Component ('Injection'). The vulnerability exists in the handling of Server-Sent Events (SSE) when streaming plain text data. An attacker can inject crafted data into the event stream, breaking message boundaries and corrupting the stream delivered to other clients. By controlling streamed content, an attacker can manipulate how subsequent events are parsed by the client, potentially altering application state or injecting misleading data.\n\n**Note:**\n\nThis is only exploitable if the application streams attacker-controlled data via SSE using unstructured/plain-text messages instead of a structured format (e.g., JSON).\n## Remediation\nUpgrade `org.springframework:spring-web` to version 6.2.17, 7.0.6 or higher.\n## References\n- [GitHub Commit](https://github.com/spring-projects/spring-framework/commit/8dc888e1b8190da93d0864c437ae945eaf06a8e9)\n- [Spring Advisory](https://spring.io/security/cve-2026-22735)\n"
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "properties": {
                "tags": [
                  "security",
                  "CWE-74",
                  "maven"
                ],
                "cvssv3_baseScore": 2.1,
                "security-severity": "2.1"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "SNYK-JAVA-ORGSPRINGFRAMEWORK-16109615",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "High severity - Incomplete Cleanup vulnerability in org.springframework:spring-web"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "(CVE-2026-22740) org.springframework:spring-web@6.1.6"
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "",
                "markdown": "## Overview\n[org.springframework:spring-web](https://github.com/spring-projects/spring-framework) is a package that provides a comprehensive programming and configuration model for modern Java-based enterprise applications - on any kind of deployment platform.\n\nAffected versions of this package are vulnerable to Incomplete Cleanup via multipart request handling in WebFlux. An attacker can exhaust disk space by sending multipart requests with large parts that trigger creation of temporary files, which under certain conditions are not deleted after the request completes, leading to accumulation of temp files and denial of service.\n## Remediation\nUpgrade `org.springframework:spring-web` to version 6.2.18, 7.0.7 or higher.\n## References\n- [GitHub Commit](https://github.com/spring-projects/spring-framework/commit/b338fdd99dd87974870f90ababb39fcb8727e1b4)\n- [spring Security Advisory](https://spring.io/security/cve-2026-22740)\n"
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "properties": {
                "tags": [
                  "security",
                  "CWE-459",
                  "maven"
                ],
                "cvssv3_baseScore": 7.1,
                "security-severity": "7.1"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "SNYK-JAVA-ORGSPRINGFRAMEWORK-17255245",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Medium severity - Cross-site Scripting (XSS) vulnerability in org.springframework:spring-web"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "(CVE-2026-41845) org.springframework:spring-web@6.1.6"
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "",
                "markdown": "## Overview\n[org.springframework:spring-web](https://github.com/spring-projects/spring-framework) is a package that provides a comprehensive programming and configuration model for modern Java-based enterprise applications - on any kind of deployment platform.\n\nAffected versions of this package are vulnerable to Cross-site Scripting (XSS) via improper escaping in `JavaScriptUtils.javaScriptEscape()`. An attacker can inject arbitrary JavaScript code into a web page when user-controlled input is escaped using `javaScriptEscape()` and subsequently embedded into a JavaScript context. Incorrect escaping may allow malicious input to break out of the intended context and execute in the victim's browser.\n## Details\n\nCross-site scripting (or XSS) is a code vulnerability that occurs when an attacker “injects” a malicious script into an otherwise trusted website. The injected script gets downloaded and executed by the end user’s browser when the user interacts with the compromised website.\n\nThis is done by escaping the context of the web application; the web application then delivers that data to its users along with other trusted dynamic content, without validating it. The browser unknowingly executes malicious script on the client side (through client-side languages; usually JavaScript or HTML)  in order to perform actions that are otherwise typically blocked by the browser’s Same Origin Policy.\n\nInjecting malicious code is the most prevalent manner by which XSS is exploited; for this reason, escaping characters in order to prevent this manipulation is the top method for securing code against this vulnerability.\n\nEscaping means that the application is coded to mark key characters, and particularly key characters included in user input, to prevent those characters from being interpreted in a dangerous context. For example, in HTML, `<` can be coded as  `&lt`; and `>` can be coded as `&gt`; in order to be interpreted and displayed as themselves in text, while within the code itself, they are used for HTML tags. If malicious content is injected into an application that escapes special characters and that malicious content uses `<` and `>` as HTML tags, those characters are nonetheless not interpreted as HTML tags by the browser if they’ve been correctly escaped in the application code and in this way the attempted attack is diverted.\n \nThe most prominent use of XSS is to steal cookies (source: OWASP HttpOnly) and hijack user sessions, but XSS exploits have been used to expose sensitive information, enable access to privileged services and functionality and deliver malware. \n\n### Types of attacks\nThere are a few methods by which XSS can be manipulated:\n\n|Type|Origin|Description|\n|--|--|--|\n|**Stored**|Server|The malicious code is inserted in the application (usually as a link) by the attacker. The code is activated every time a user clicks the link.|\n|**Reflected**|Server|The attacker delivers a malicious link externally from the vulnerable web site application to a user. When clicked, malicious code is sent to the vulnerable web site, which reflects the attack back to the user’s browser.| \n|**DOM-based**|Client|The attacker forces the user’s browser to render a malicious page. The data in the page itself delivers the cross-site scripting data.|\n|**Mutated**| |The attacker injects code that appears safe, but is then rewritten and modified by the browser, while parsing the markup. An example is rebalancing unclosed quotation marks or even adding quotation marks to unquoted parameters.|\n\n### Affected environments\nThe following environments are susceptible to an XSS attack:\n\n* Web servers\n* Application servers\n* Web application environments\n\n### How to prevent\nThis section describes the top best practices designed to specifically protect your code: \n\n* Sanitize data input in an HTTP request before reflecting it back, ensuring all data is validated, filtered or escaped before echoing anything back to the user, such as the values of query parameters during searches. \n* Convert special characters such as `?`, `&`, `/`, `<`, `>` and spaces to their respective HTML or URL encoded equivalents. \n* Give users the option to disable client-side scripts.\n* Redirect invalid requests.\n* Detect simultaneous logins, including those from two separate IP addresses, and invalidate those sessions.\n* Use and enforce a Content Security Policy (source: Wikipedia) to disable any features that might be manipulated for an XSS attack.\n* Read the documentation for any of the libraries referenced in your code to understand which elements allow for embedded HTML.\n\n## Remediation\nUpgrade `org.springframework:spring-web` to version 6.0.0, 6.2.19, 7.0.8 or higher.\n## References\n- [GitHub Commit](https://github.com/spring-projects/spring-framework/commit/86d99790dbaa8ce6bb1087ef92844d0abfdab015)\n- [GitHub Release](https://github.com/spring-projects/spring-framework/releases/tag/v6.2.19)\n- [GitHub Release](https://github.com/spring-projects/spring-framework/releases/tag/v7.0.8)\n- [Spring Security Advisory](https://spring.io/security/cve-2026-41845)\n"
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "properties": {
                "tags": [
                  "security",
                  "CWE-79",
                  "maven"
                ],
                "cvssv3_baseScore": 5.3,
                "security-severity": "5.3"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "SNYK-JAVA-ORGSPRINGFRAMEWORK-19267076",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Medium severity - HTTP Response Splitting vulnerability in org.springframework:spring-web"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "(CVE-2026-59314) org.springframework:spring-web@6.1.6"
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "",
                "markdown": "## Overview\n[org.springframework:spring-web](https://github.com/spring-projects/spring-framework) is a package that provides a comprehensive programming and configuration model for modern Java-based enterprise applications - on any kind of deployment platform.\n\nAffected versions of this package are vulnerable to HTTP Response Splitting via the `Content-Disposition` header when untrusted input is used to construct its value. An attacker can inject malicious characters to break the HTTP header or corrupt the framing of an outbound multipart body by supplying specially crafted file names or values. \n\n**Note:** This is only exploitable if the application uses non-default or legacy HTTP connectors that do not reject malicious characters in header values, or if untrusted input is used to set the `Content-Disposition` of a part in an outbound multipart request body.\n## Remediation\nUpgrade `org.springframework:spring-web` to version 7.0.9 or higher.\n## References\n- [GitHub Commit](https://github.com/spring-projects/spring-framework/commit/8fb2f72282a94f7029673284aef0adb035cae2a7)\n- [Spring Security Advisory](https://spring.io/security/cve-2026-59314)\n"
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "properties": {
                "tags": [
                  "security",
                  "CWE-113",
                  "maven"
                ],
                "cvssv3_baseScore": 6.3,
                "security-severity": "6.3"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "SNYK-JAVA-ORGSPRINGFRAMEWORK-19267077",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "High severity - Allocation of Resources Without Limits or Throttling vulnerability in org.springframework:spring-web"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "(CVE-2026-47885) org.springframework:spring-web@6.1.6"
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "",
                "markdown": "## Overview\n[org.springframework:spring-web](https://github.com/spring-projects/spring-framework) is a package that provides a comprehensive programming and configuration model for modern Java-based enterprise applications - on any kind of deployment platform.\n\nAffected versions of this package are vulnerable to Allocation of Resources Without Limits or Throttling in the `PartEventHttpMessageReader` file when `maxInMemorySize` is set to -1. An attacker can cause excessive memory consumption by uploading large multipart requests.\n\n**Note:** This is only exploitable if the configuration explicitly sets `maxInMemorySize` to -1.\n## Remediation\nUpgrade `org.springframework:spring-web` to version 7.0.9 or higher.\n## References\n- [GitHub Commit](https://github.com/spring-projects/spring-framework/commit/8647e90bc7b2da9b299566296f2b253a6fd9c128)\n- [Spring Security Advisory](https://spring.io/security/cve-2026-47885)\n"
              },
