            {
              "id": "SNYK-JAVA-ORGSPRINGFRAMEWORK-17254527",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "High severity - Direct Request ('Forced Browsing') vulnerability in org.springframework:spring-webmvc"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "(CVE-2026-41841) org.springframework:spring-webmvc@6.1.6"
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "",
                "markdown": "## Overview\n[org.springframework:spring-webmvc](https://mvnrepository.com/artifact/org.springframework/spring-webmvc) is a package that provides Model-View-Controller (MVC) architecture and ready components that can be used to develop flexible and loosely coupled web applications.\n\nAffected versions of this package are vulnerable to Direct Request ('Forced Browsing') via shared caching of static resource resolutions across resource handlers. An attacker can gain unauthorized access to protected resources when a shared cache stores a resource resolution result from a publicly accessible handler and subsequently reuses it for a protected handler serving a resource with the same name. This can cause resources that should require authentication to be served without proper access control checks.\r\n\r\n**Note:** This is only exploitable if the application uses Spring MVC or Spring WebFlux, configures multiple resource handlers with different resource locations, protects at least one handler with authentication, and uses a shared cache for resource resolution.\n## Remediation\nUpgrade `org.springframework:spring-webmvc` to version 6.0.0, 6.2.19, 7.0.8 or higher.\n## References\n- [GitHub Commit](https://github.com/spring-projects/spring-framework/commit/46867fad81dc8a3c9552d96750f5e37b1a4edd75)\n- [GitHub Release](https://github.com/spring-projects/spring-framework/releases/tag/v6.2.19)\n- [GitHub Release](https://github.com/spring-projects/spring-framework/releases/tag/v7.0.8)\n- [Spring Security Advisory](https://spring.io/security/cve-2026-41841)\n"
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "properties": {
                "tags": [
                  "security",
                  "CWE-425",
                  "maven"
                ],
                "cvssv3_baseScore": 8.2,
                "security-severity": "8.2"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "SNYK-JAVA-ORGSPRINGFRAMEWORK-17254544",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "High severity - Allocation of Resources Without Limits or Throttling vulnerability in org.springframework:spring-webmvc"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "(CVE-2026-41842) org.springframework:spring-webmvc@6.1.6"
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "",
                "markdown": "## Overview\n[org.springframework:spring-webmvc](https://mvnrepository.com/artifact/org.springframework/spring-webmvc) is a package that provides Model-View-Controller (MVC) architecture and ready components that can be used to develop flexible and loosely coupled web applications.\n\nAffected versions of this package are vulnerable to Allocation of Resources Without Limits or Throttling via static resource resolution when versioned resource support is enabled. An attacker can cause denial of service by sending crafted requests that trigger expensive resource resolution operations against filesystem-backed static resources. Repeated requests can consume server resources and keep HTTP connections occupied for extended periods, potentially degrading performance or rendering the application unavailable.\r\n\r\n**Note:** This is only exploitable if the application uses Spring MVC or Spring WebFlux, serves static resources from the filesystem, and has versioned resource support enabled.\n## Remediation\nUpgrade `org.springframework:spring-webmvc` to version 6.0.0, 6.2.19, 7.0.8 or higher.\n## References\n- [GitHub Commit](https://github.com/spring-projects/spring-framework/commit/fb0c78ae27c4cea1c6b9a9c58b3cad77233965d5)\n- [GitHub Release](https://github.com/spring-projects/spring-framework/releases/tag/v6.2.19)\n- [GitHub Release](https://github.com/spring-projects/spring-framework/releases/tag/v7.0.8)\n- [Spring Security Advisory](https://spring.io/security/cve-2026-41842)\n"
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "properties": {
                "tags": [
                  "security",
                  "CWE-770",
                  "maven"
                ],
                "cvssv3_baseScore": 8.2,
                "security-severity": "8.2"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "SNYK-JAVA-ORGSPRINGFRAMEWORK-18326607",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Medium severity - HTTP Request Smuggling vulnerability in org.springframework:spring-webmvc"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "(CVE-2026-41853) org.springframework:spring-webmvc@6.1.6"
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "",
                "markdown": "## Overview\n\n[org.springframework:spring-webmvc](https://mvnrepository.com/artifact/org.springframework/spring-webmvc) is a package that provides Model-View-Controller (MVC) architecture and ready components that can be used to develop flexible and loosely coupled web applications.\n\n\nAffected versions of this package are vulnerable to HTTP Request Smuggling.\nvia multipart request parsing discrepancies between Spring MVC/WebFlux and intermediary security devices. An attacker can bypass Web Application Firewall (WAF) or proxy security controls by sending crafted multipart requests that are interpreted differently by the intermediary and the Spring application, allowing malicious content to evade inspection and reach the backend application.\n\n## Remediation\n\nUpgrade `org.springframework:spring-webmvc` to version 6.0.0, 6.2.19, 7.0.8 or higher.\n\n\n## References\n\n- [GitHub Commit](https://github.com/spring-projects/spring-framework/commit/a58fdeaf3fc1b8edaa3f42a6679df133e318df0e)\n\n- [GitHub Release](https://github.com/spring-projects/spring-framework/releases/tag/v6.2.19)\n\n- [GitHub Release](https://github.com/spring-projects/spring-framework/releases/tag/v7.0.8)\n\n- [Spring Security Advisory](https://spring.io/security/cve-2026-41853)\n"
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "properties": {
                "tags": [
                  "security",
                  "CWE-444",
                  "maven"
                ],
                "cvssv3_baseScore": 6.9,
                "security-severity": "6.9"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "SNYK-JAVA-ORGSPRINGFRAMEWORK-19267098",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Critical severity - Arbitrary Code Injection vulnerability in org.springframework:spring-webmvc"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "(CVE-2026-47884) org.springframework:spring-webmvc@6.1.6"
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "",
                "markdown": "## Overview\n[org.springframework:spring-webmvc](https://mvnrepository.com/artifact/org.springframework/spring-webmvc) is a package that provides Model-View-Controller (MVC) architecture and ready components that can be used to develop flexible and loosely coupled web applications.\n\nAffected versions of this package are vulnerable to Arbitrary Code Injection via the `XsltView` file when an application has a `/**` mapping that results in view rendering and the view name is not explicitly specified. An attacker can execute arbitrary code or make unauthorized network requests by supplying crafted input to manipulate the view resolution process.\n\n**Note:** This is only exploitable if the application is configured with a `/**` mapping that triggers view rendering without explicitly specifying the view name.\n## Remediation\nUpgrade `org.springframework:spring-webmvc` to version 7.0.9 or higher.\n## References\n- [GitHub Commit](https://github.com/spring-projects/spring-framework/commit/692dbc9160de3b5de50ccedeee014716d0cedb7b)\n- [Spring Security Advisory](https://spring.io/security/cve-2026-47884)\n"
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "properties": {
                "tags": [
                  "security",
                  "CWE-94",
                  "maven"
                ],
                "cvssv3_baseScore": 9.1,
                "security-severity": "9.1"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "SNYK-JAVA-ORGSPRINGFRAMEWORK-19267099",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Medium severity - Open Redirect vulnerability in org.springframework:spring-webmvc"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "(CVE-2026-47887) org.springframework:spring-webmvc@6.1.6"
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "",
                "markdown": "## Overview\n[org.springframework:spring-webmvc](https://mvnrepository.com/artifact/org.springframework/spring-webmvc) is a package that provides Model-View-Controller (MVC) architecture and ready components that can be used to develop flexible and loosely coupled web applications.\n\nAffected versions of this package are vulnerable to Open Redirect in the `UrlFileNameViewController` file when it is mapped with an end-of-path and lacks a configured prefix. An attacker can redirect users to arbitrary external URLs by crafting a specially constructed request.\n## Remediation\nUpgrade `org.springframework:spring-webmvc` to version 7.0.9 or higher.\n## References\n- [GitHub Commit](https://github.com/spring-projects/spring-framework/commit/b9379e33d52b491e227715776a072d07bcccddab)\n- [Spring Security Advisory](https://spring.io/security/cve-2026-47887)\n"
              },
