            {
              "id": "SNYK-JAVA-ORGSPRINGFRAMEWORKBOOT-9804539",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Medium severity - Improper Input Validation vulnerability in org.springframework.boot:spring-boot-actuator-autoconfigure"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "(CVE-2025-22235) org.springframework.boot:spring-boot-actuator-autoconfigure@3.2.5"
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "",
                "markdown": "## Overview\n\nAffected versions of this package are vulnerable to Improper Input Validation via the `EndpointRequest.to()` function that creates a matcher for `null/**` if the actuator endpoint, for which the `EndpointRequest` has been created, is disabled or not exposed.\r\n\r\n**Note:**\r\n\r\nThis is only exploitable if all of the following conditions are met:\r\n\r\n1) `EndpointRequest.to()` has been used in a Spring Security chain configuration;\r\n\r\n2) The endpoint which `EndpointRequest` references is disabled or not exposed via web;\r\n\r\n3) Your application handles requests to `/null` and this path needs protection.\r\n\r\n## Workaround\r\n\r\nThis can be mitigated by either:\r\n\r\n1) Making sure that the endpoint to which `EndpointRequest.to()` is referring to is enabled and exposed via web;\r\n\r\n2) Make sure that you don't handle requests to `/null`.\n## Remediation\nUpgrade `org.springframework.boot:spring-boot-actuator-autoconfigure` to version 3.3.11, 3.4.5 or higher.\n## References\n- [GitHub Commit](https://github.com/spring-projects/spring-boot/commit/55f67c9a522647039fd3294dee5cb83f4888160a)\n- [Spring Security Advisory](https://spring.io/security/cve-2025-22235)\n"
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "properties": {
                "tags": [
                  "security",
                  "CWE-20",
                  "maven"
                ],
                "cvssv3_baseScore": 6.9,
                "security-severity": "6.9"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "SNYK-JAVA-ORGSPRINGFRAMEWORKBOOT-15701836",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Critical severity - Authentication Bypass Using an Alternate Path or Channel vulnerability in org.springframework.boot:spring-boot-actuator"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "(CVE-2026-22733) org.springframework.boot:spring-boot-actuator@3.2.5"
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "",
                "markdown": "## Overview\n\nAffected versions of this package are vulnerable to Authentication Bypass Using an Alternate Path or Channel via the Actuator CloudFoundry endpoints. An attacker can gain unauthorized access to protected endpoints by sending requests to application endpoints declared under the CloudFoundry Actuator path.\r\n\r\n**Note:**\r\n\r\nThis is only exploitable if all of the following conditions are met:\r\n\r\n- the application is a web application\r\n\r\n- the application contributes an application endpoint that requires authentication under a subpath, like `\"/cloudfoundryapplication/admin\"`\n## Remediation\nUpgrade `org.springframework.boot:spring-boot-actuator` to version 3.5.12, 4.0.4 or higher.\n## References\n- [GitHub Commit](https://github.com/spring-projects/spring-boot/commit/01fbede2b27237616e215fe0df7c294ae47bdd73)\n- [Spring Advisory](https://spring.io/security/cve-2026-22733)\n"
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "properties": {
                "tags": [
                  "security",
                  "CWE-288",
                  "maven"
                ],
                "cvssv3_baseScore": 9.2,
                "security-severity": "9.2"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "SNYK-JAVA-ORGSPRINGFRAMEWORKBOOT-16191022",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Critical severity - Improper Validation of Certificate with Host Mismatch vulnerability in org.springframework.boot:spring-boot-autoconfigure"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "(CVE-2026-40974) org.springframework.boot:spring-boot-autoconfigure@3.2.5"
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "",
                "markdown": "## Overview\n\nAffected versions of this package are vulnerable to Improper Validation of Certificate with Host Mismatch due to establishing SSL connections to Cassandra without verifying that the hostname in the server's SSL certificate actually matched the hostname of the server being connected to. While the application might have verified that the certificate was signed by a trusted Certificate Authority (CA), failing to verify the hostname means an attacker could present any valid certificate (even one meant for a different domain) to successfully intercept the connection, leaving the application vulnerable to Man-in-the-Middle (MitM) attacks.\n## Remediation\nUpgrade `org.springframework.boot:spring-boot-autoconfigure` to version 3.5.14, 4.0.6 or higher.\n## References\n- [GitHub Commit](https://github.com/spring-projects/spring-boot/commit/e22083a5684c3c65bcf2a9a90adcdecee6e85d50)\n- [Spring Security Advisory](https://spring.io/security/cve-2026-40974)\n"
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "properties": {
                "tags": [
                  "security",
                  "CWE-297",
                  "maven"
                ],
                "cvssv3_baseScore": 9.3,
                "security-severity": "9.3"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "SNYK-JAVA-ORGSPRINGFRAMEWORKBOOT-16200231",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Critical severity - Improper Validation of Certificate with Host Mismatch vulnerability in org.springframework.boot:spring-boot-autoconfigure"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "(CVE-2026-40971) org.springframework.boot:spring-boot-autoconfigure@3.2.5"
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "",
                "markdown": "## Overview\n\nAffected versions of this package are vulnerable to Improper Validation of Certificate with Host Mismatch when using an SSL bundle. This effectively weakens TLS by allowing connections without verifying the server identity (classic MITM risk).\n## Remediation\nUpgrade `org.springframework.boot:spring-boot-autoconfigure` to version 3.5.14, 4.0.6 or higher.\n## References\n- [GitHub Commit](https://github.com/spring-projects/spring-boot/commit/e4febe2015d340ea9135437ee0659ea0f2260c31)\n- [Spring Security Advisory](https://spring.io/security/cve-2026-40971)\n"
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "properties": {
                "tags": [
                  "security",
                  "CWE-297",
                  "maven"
                ],
                "cvssv3_baseScore": 9.2,
                "security-severity": "9.2"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "SNYK-JAVA-ORGSPRINGFRAMEWORKBOOT-17308346",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Medium severity - Insecure Temporary File vulnerability in org.springframework.boot:spring-boot-autoconfigure"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "(CVE-2026-41001) org.springframework.boot:spring-boot-autoconfigure@3.2.5"
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "",
                "markdown": "## Overview\n\nAffected versions of this package are vulnerable to Insecure Temporary File via the default data directory configuration in `ArtemisEmbeddedConfigurationFactory`. A local attacker can tamper with or redirect the embedded Artemis broker's data storage by pre-creating the predictable data directory or replacing it with a symlink before the application starts. This may allow unauthorized access to message data, injection of malicious messages, or further compromise through processing of attacker-controlled broker data.\r\n\r\n**Note:** This is only exploitable by an attacker with local access to the host system before the application initializes the embedded broker.\n## Remediation\nUpgrade `org.springframework.boot:spring-boot-autoconfigure` to version 3.5.15, 4.0.7, 4.1.0 or higher.\n## References\n- [GitHub Commit](https://github.com/spring-projects/spring-boot/commit/4218bd76e934e5cf9e3fd3997c67b8a6b0d0c111)\n- [Spring Security Advisory](https://spring.io/security/cve-2026-41001)\n"
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "properties": {
                "tags": [
                  "security",
                  "CWE-377",
                  "maven"
                ],
                "cvssv3_baseScore": 4.8,
                "security-severity": "4.8"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "SNYK-JAVA-ORGSPRINGFRAMEWORKBOOT-16191649",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "High severity - Use of Cryptographically Weak Pseudo-Random Number Generator (PRNG) vulnerability in org.springframework.boot:spring-boot"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "(CVE-2026-40975) org.springframework.boot:spring-boot@3.2.5"
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "",
                "markdown": "## Overview\n\nAffected versions of this package are vulnerable to Use of Cryptographically Weak Pseudo-Random Number Generator (PRNG) for the property source for `${random.value}` (as well as `${random.int}` and `${random.long}`). Standard PRNGs (like `java.util.Random`) use deterministic mathematical algorithms starting from a seed value. Because the state space is relatively small and lacks ongoing entropy (true randomness), an attacker who observes a sequence of generated values can mathematically reverse-engineer the seed. Once the seed is known, the attacker can predict all past and future values generated by that PRNG. If these values are used to generate security-sensitive assets like API keys, session tokens, or passwords, the system becomes compromised.\n## Remediation\nUpgrade `org.springframework.boot:spring-boot` to version 3.5.14, 4.0.6 or higher.\n## References\n- [GitHub Commit](https://github.com/spring-projects/spring-boot/commit/f3b8eb0f2cd989dffe5dceefce80bde165328b31)\n- [Spring Security Advisory](https://spring.io/security/cve-2026-40975)\n"
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "properties": {
                "tags": [
                  "security",
                  "CWE-338",
                  "maven"
                ],
                "cvssv3_baseScore": 8.2,
                "security-severity": "8.2"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "SNYK-JAVA-ORGSPRINGFRAMEWORKBOOT-16198880",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "High severity - Insecure Temporary File vulnerability in org.springframework.boot:spring-boot"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "(CVE-2026-40973) org.springframework.boot:spring-boot@3.2.5"
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "",
                "markdown": "## Overview\n\nAffected versions of this package are vulnerable to Insecure Temporary File due to the `ApplicationTemp` mechanism creating a temporary directory using a predictable name. Because the name can be easily guessed, a local attacker on the same server can maliciously pre-create this directory before the Spring Boot application starts. When the application launches, it would blindly use the existing directory without verifying if it is actually owned by the application's user or the attacker.\n## Remediation\nUpgrade `org.springframework.boot:spring-boot` to version 3.5.14, 4.0.6 or higher.\n## References\n- [GitHub Commit](https://github.com/spring-projects/spring-boot/commit/5ceb1a228932e35cc803d1c1fea68f0f984aaa90)\n- [Spring Security Advisory](https://spring.io/security/cve-2026-40973)\n"
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "properties": {
                "tags": [
                  "security",
                  "CWE-377",
                  "maven"
                ],
                "cvssv3_baseScore": 7.3,
                "security-severity": "7.3"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "SNYK-JAVA-ORGSPRINGFRAMEWORKBOOT-16201011",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Medium severity - Symlink Attack vulnerability in org.springframework.boot:spring-boot"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "(CVE-2026-40977) org.springframework.boot:spring-boot@3.2.5"
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "",
                "markdown": "## Overview\n\nAffected versions of this package are vulnerable to Symlink Attack due to insecure handling of Process ID (PID) files. When an application uses the `ApplicationPidFileWriter`, it writes its PID to a predictable file system path. A local attacker with write access to the PID file's directory can create a symbolic link (symlink) at that path. When the Spring Boot application starts, it follows this symlink and overwrites the target file with its PID. This allows the attacker to corrupt or \"clobber\" sensitive system files, potentially leading to a denial of service or system instability.\n## Remediation\nUpgrade `org.springframework.boot:spring-boot` to version 3.5.14, 4.0.6 or higher.\n## References\n- [GitHub Commit](https://github.com/spring-projects/spring-boot/commit/f533a4549c3999aac30cb5830f07dc304933e93d)\n- [Spring Security Advisory](https://spring.io/security/cve-2026-40977)\n"
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "properties": {
                "tags": [
                  "security",
                  "CWE-59",
                  "maven"
                ],
                "cvssv3_baseScore": 5.7,
                "security-severity": "5.7"
              }
            }
          ]
        }
      },
